# Shell scripts run as container entrypoints/commands on Linux — a mangled shebang
# (e.g. CRLF from a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true, turning "#!/bin/bash"
# into "#!/bin/bash\r") breaks them with a confusing "exec: no such file or directory"
# error. Force LF regardless of platform or local autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf

# infra/plugin-mirror/: vendored third-party plugin build, distributed byte-for-byte
# to end users' Obsidian installs. CRLF wouldn't break JS parsing the way it broke
# the shell scripts above, but there's no reason to risk it or diff noise either —
# keep these exactly as vendored.
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
